# Lint After Code Generation

After any substantive code change (new files, edits, refactors):

1. Run `pnpm lint` before considering the task done.
2. Fix every reported error (and warning when easy).
3. Re-run `pnpm lint` until it exits with code 0.
4. If `--fix` can safely resolve an issue, use it, then re-check.

Do not skip this step for "small" edits. Do not report completion while lint fails.
